1
00:00:33,408 --> 00:00:34,652
Who was it?

2
00:00:35,320 --> 00:00:37,328
I said, who was it!

3
00:00:40,380 --> 00:00:42,167
Was it you?

4
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:43,979
Was it you? Kim Jin Mi, answer.

5
00:00:43,979 --> 00:00:46,993
- It's not that...
- Answer me!

6
00:00:46,993 --> 00:00:48,840
It's fine, Yu Gyeom...

7
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:51,178
I asked you a question, Kim Jin Mi.

8
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:53,086
Well, I...

9
00:00:53,086 --> 00:00:55,260
I wanted Sung Sae Ryeong...

10
00:00:55,260 --> 00:00:57,212
She's the one I called over...

11
00:00:57,900 --> 00:01:01,456
So you meant to do this to Sae Ryeong?

12
00:01:01,456 --> 00:01:02,489
Why?

13
00:01:02,489 --> 00:01:04,429
Because we broke up?

14
00:01:04,429 --> 00:01:07,636
You're so low, it makes me sick.

15
00:01:07,636 --> 00:01:09,063
I'm sorry!

16
00:01:09,063 --> 00:01:11,176
This was stupid of me.

17
00:01:11,176 --> 00:01:13,446
But Sung Sae Ryeong was horrible to us!

18
00:01:13,446 --> 00:01:14,722
That's why we did it.

19
00:01:14,722 --> 00:01:18,484
So, your girlfriend...
was never meant to be the target!

20
00:01:18,484 --> 00:01:20,502
I'm so sorry!

21
00:01:20,502 --> 00:01:22,661
And she can wash it off, you know!

22
00:01:22,661 --> 00:01:24,742
It'll come right off.

23
00:01:26,316 --> 00:01:27,938
Wash it off?

24
00:01:28,976 --> 00:01:31,569
- I'll take her and get it off right now!
- Jin Mi.

25
00:01:31,569 --> 00:01:33,115
Give me your phone.

26
00:01:35,376 --> 00:01:37,469
M-My phone?

27
00:01:37,469 --> 00:01:40,112
Do I have to pry it from you,
or will you give it over?

28
00:01:50,736 --> 00:01:52,273
What did you just do?

29
00:01:52,273 --> 00:01:53,697
What's wrong? You can just fix it.

30
00:01:53,697 --> 00:01:55,648
Just like she can wash it off.

31
00:02:01,249 --> 00:02:02,969
Hey, Cho Yu Gyeom.

32
00:02:02,969 --> 00:02:04,207
Go ahead.

33
00:02:04,207 --> 00:02:07,032
You don't know when to stop, do you?

34
00:02:07,763 --> 00:02:10,773
I was used and abused by Sung Sae Ryeong!

35
00:02:10,773 --> 00:02:13,229
I was basically her servant for four years!

36
00:02:13,229 --> 00:02:15,686
She was a monster!

37
00:02:15,686 --> 00:02:17,417
And you dated her, didn't you?

38
00:02:17,417 --> 00:02:20,909
You know what a witch she is!

39
00:02:20,909 --> 00:02:23,846
I'm sorry for what I did
to your current girlfriend,

40
00:02:23,846 --> 00:02:26,430
but you're going too far!

41
00:02:26,430 --> 00:02:29,247
Let's be honest, you dated Sae Ryeong and
Ha Yeon at the same time,

42
00:02:29,247 --> 00:02:32,089
and look where it got all of us!

43
00:02:32,089 --> 00:02:33,416
Hey!

44
00:02:33,416 --> 00:02:34,806
You know what my mom said?

45
00:02:34,806 --> 00:02:36,489
That's what happened with your family.

46
00:02:36,489 --> 00:02:38,540
Everyone in this town knows how it goes.

47
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:40,452
You and your sisters are from different lovers!

48
00:02:40,452 --> 00:02:42,215
Kim Jin Mi.

49
00:02:45,730 --> 00:02:48,299
I heard you smell like rotten fish.

50
00:02:49,711 --> 00:02:51,634
- What?
- Your boyfriend...

51
00:02:51,634 --> 00:02:53,522
Lee Won Bae told me.

52
00:02:57,856 --> 00:02:59,012
What?

53
00:02:59,012 --> 00:03:00,708
Jin Mi.

54
00:03:01,503 --> 00:03:03,130
We're all trash.

55
00:03:04,023 --> 00:03:06,436
A heap of trash that only gets worse
the deeper you dig.

56
00:03:06,436 --> 00:03:08,513
We stink like hell.

57
00:03:09,516 --> 00:03:11,024
Well...

58
00:03:11,024 --> 00:03:13,172
The stench isn't the worst of it.

59
00:03:15,163 --> 00:03:17,590
And yet...

60
00:03:17,590 --> 00:03:21,243
we all go on pretending we're not.
So why can't you?

61
00:03:21,243 --> 00:03:25,622
I don't understand why...
you want to prove that we are all trash!

62
00:03:25,622 --> 00:03:27,191
You hear me? We're trash!

63
00:03:27,191 --> 00:03:30,461
You're rotten fish,
and I'm dust from a wrecked home!

64
00:03:35,790 --> 00:03:39,099
Is this... what you wanted to hear?

65
00:04:04,110 --> 00:04:05,134
[Namsu - Upo - Upo CC]

66
00:04:05,134 --> 00:04:09,230
[5. Road Bound Home]

67
00:04:09,230 --> 00:04:10,745
[Episode 5]

68
00:04:15,339 --> 00:04:18,363
<i>In my family, only Mom is mine.</i>

69
00:04:18,363 --> 00:04:19,820
<i>That's what happened with your family.</i>

70
00:04:19,820 --> 00:04:22,702
<i>You and your sisters are from different lovers!</i>

71
00:04:33,543 --> 00:04:35,609
You don't smell.

72
00:04:35,609 --> 00:04:37,402
Really, you don't.

73
00:04:37,402 --> 00:04:38,703
But...

74
00:04:38,703 --> 00:04:40,390
I keep smelling something.

75
00:04:40,390 --> 00:04:41,905
I can't smell it at all.

76
00:04:42,876 --> 00:04:44,618
Really?

77
00:04:44,618 --> 00:04:45,784
Yeah.

78
00:04:46,745 --> 00:04:48,299
Are you okay?

79
00:04:50,457 --> 00:04:53,783
I think I should be the one asking that.

80
00:04:53,783 --> 00:04:55,676
Of course I'm fine.

81
00:04:57,464 --> 00:04:58,994
Yeah. I'm fine.

82
00:05:00,216 --> 00:05:04,830
I had no idea what you meant about your mom.

83
00:05:06,723 --> 00:05:08,722
Nobody does, at first.

84
00:05:09,370 --> 00:05:10,734
It's okay.

85
00:05:12,923 --> 00:05:14,989
Why are you looking at me like that?

86
00:05:14,989 --> 00:05:16,982
It's just fascinating.

87
00:05:16,982 --> 00:05:18,607
What is?

88
00:05:20,503 --> 00:05:22,103
Actually...

89
00:05:22,103 --> 00:05:25,835
I've always wanted to be a protagonist
with a mysterious past.

90
00:05:25,835 --> 00:05:27,158
What?

91
00:05:29,890 --> 00:05:32,510
My mom's just straight-up evil.

92
00:05:32,510 --> 00:05:35,729
So I'd often wish she wasn't my real mom.

93
00:05:36,423 --> 00:05:39,756
Every family has at least one evil person.

94
00:05:39,756 --> 00:05:42,543
- Does yours have one, too?
- Of course we do.

95
00:05:43,896 --> 00:05:45,887
I...

96
00:05:45,887 --> 00:05:48,167
absolutely despise my mom.

97
00:05:48,167 --> 00:05:49,523
Why?

98
00:05:49,523 --> 00:05:50,690
Just because.

99
00:05:50,690 --> 00:05:52,888
I don't want to end up like her.

100
00:05:54,503 --> 00:05:57,941
I'm scared of becoming my dad, too.

101
00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:01,200
What about movies?

102
00:06:02,940 --> 00:06:05,267
Do you like movies?

103
00:06:06,593 --> 00:06:08,320
I do.

104
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:09,580
Me too.

105
00:06:09,580 --> 00:06:11,540
I like them too.

106
00:06:11,540 --> 00:06:13,600
What is this?

107
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:15,430
Things we have in common.

108
00:06:16,210 --> 00:06:17,313
What?

109
00:06:17,313 --> 00:06:19,840
Things we have in common!

110
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:21,740
You're cute.

111
00:06:21,740 --> 00:06:24,213
I didn't start it, okay?

112
00:06:24,213 --> 00:06:26,565
She's the one who started it!

113
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:29,710
I'm not lying!

114
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:38,726
Hey.

115
00:06:38,726 --> 00:06:41,233
She's a minor, you hear? A minor!

116
00:06:41,233 --> 00:06:42,966
Legally underage!

117
00:06:42,966 --> 00:06:45,380
Do you miss being in prison?

118
00:06:45,380 --> 00:06:47,840
You just got out. Already at it again?

119
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:49,197
I told you already.

120
00:06:49,197 --> 00:06:50,946
It wasn't my fault!

121
00:06:50,946 --> 00:06:53,830
The tramp approached me first, I swear!

122
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:55,606
Hey, you.

123
00:06:55,606 --> 00:06:57,750
One more strike, and you're out.

124
00:06:57,750 --> 00:06:58,961
Damn it...

125
00:06:58,961 --> 00:07:01,204
But I swear it wasn't me, I...

126
00:07:02,626 --> 00:07:04,341
I'm sure you know what happens
after strike three.

127
00:07:04,341 --> 00:07:06,267
You have to believe me.

128
00:07:06,267 --> 00:07:08,953
Please, you have to believe me!

129
00:07:08,953 --> 00:07:11,421
You can't believe someone you don't trust.

130
00:07:12,745 --> 00:07:14,000
Got it?

131
00:07:15,186 --> 00:07:17,100
I have three sisters.

132
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:19,033
Not one?

133
00:07:19,033 --> 00:07:20,326
Yeah.

134
00:07:20,326 --> 00:07:21,600
Three.

135
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:24,833
I had no idea. I only saw one of them.

136
00:07:24,833 --> 00:07:25,890
That's the third one.

137
00:07:25,890 --> 00:07:27,256
Sam Hee.

138
00:07:28,113 --> 00:07:29,766
And?

139
00:07:29,766 --> 00:07:32,005
The first one got married.

140
00:07:33,013 --> 00:07:35,580
What about the middle one?

141
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:37,491
I don't know. She ran away.

142
00:07:38,193 --> 00:07:40,380
- Hello, miss!
- Good morning, miss!

143
00:07:40,380 --> 00:07:41,917
She's somewhere, at least.

144
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:46,413
- Morning, miss!
- Hello, miss!

145
00:07:54,013 --> 00:07:55,380
Hey, boss.

146
00:07:55,380 --> 00:07:57,004
She says she didn't get any money yesterday.

147
00:07:57,004 --> 00:08:00,122
She left early because of her period cramps.

148
00:08:11,846 --> 00:08:13,226
You, girl.

149
00:08:13,226 --> 00:08:14,946
Give me the phone number.

150
00:08:14,946 --> 00:08:15,971
Pardon me?

151
00:08:15,971 --> 00:08:17,277
What number?

152
00:08:17,277 --> 00:08:19,666
The guy who runs the place you worked at.

153
00:08:19,666 --> 00:08:20,998
Spit it out.

154
00:08:22,261 --> 00:08:23,361
That's...

155
00:08:23,361 --> 00:08:24,703
Hey!

156
00:08:24,703 --> 00:08:26,931
You did work, right?

157
00:08:26,931 --> 00:08:29,336
You should get paid for every hour you worked.

158
00:08:29,336 --> 00:08:31,664
Cutting it short doesn't mean
you shouldn't get paid.

159
00:08:32,633 --> 00:08:33,873
Hey.

160
00:08:33,873 --> 00:08:36,849
I'll call the owner for you,
so give me the number.

161
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:39,023
Come on!

162
00:08:42,653 --> 00:08:44,464
I asked for a number, not money.

163
00:08:44,464 --> 00:08:46,447
Whatever!

164
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:50,400
Unbelievable!

165
00:08:51,733 --> 00:08:55,385
Kids these days, lying through their teeth!

166
00:08:56,906 --> 00:08:57,993
Hey!

167
00:08:57,993 --> 00:09:00,290
How did you know she was lying?

168
00:09:00,290 --> 00:09:02,130
She almost fooled me!

169
00:09:05,170 --> 00:09:06,922
Hey.

170
00:09:06,922 --> 00:09:08,805
She says she's new.

171
00:09:12,302 --> 00:09:15,430
I heard you can help minors get jobs.

172
00:09:15,430 --> 00:09:17,208
I need to make money.

173
00:09:19,103 --> 00:09:20,602
Hey, girl.

174
00:09:20,602 --> 00:09:22,994
We can help, but...

175
00:09:22,994 --> 00:09:24,430
[Sung Sae Ryeong]
Lots.

176
00:09:24,430 --> 00:09:26,303
Lots and lots of money.

177
00:09:26,303 --> 00:09:28,167
I'll take any kind of job.

178
00:09:28,167 --> 00:09:31,292
I just need it to pay well.

179
00:09:31,292 --> 00:09:32,316
You'll do anything?

180
00:09:32,316 --> 00:09:34,107
Yes, anything at all.

181
00:09:34,107 --> 00:09:35,271
Everything.

182
00:09:35,271 --> 00:09:38,537
I hope you don't have the wrong idea.

183
00:09:38,537 --> 00:09:40,289
Let me just say...

184
00:09:41,830 --> 00:09:44,438
Even really shady stuff is fine.

185
00:09:48,172 --> 00:09:49,623
Crazy.

186
00:09:51,510 --> 00:09:52,634
Why are you laughing?

187
00:09:52,634 --> 00:09:54,167
I'm desperate.

188
00:09:55,616 --> 00:09:57,210
I know.

189
00:09:57,210 --> 00:09:59,316
We know how you feel, but...

190
00:10:02,843 --> 00:10:04,516
Hey.

191
00:10:04,516 --> 00:10:06,676
Do you have a place to stay?

192
00:10:06,676 --> 00:10:10,763
We get so many runaways here.
It's blatantly obvious.

193
00:10:10,763 --> 00:10:12,103
Hey, Jeong Min!

194
00:10:12,103 --> 00:10:15,210
Call Mi Young and get this girl a room.

195
00:10:17,170 --> 00:10:18,202
And you.

196
00:10:18,202 --> 00:10:21,150
I'll be in touch,
so stay there and don't go anywhere.

197
00:10:21,150 --> 00:10:22,710
Got it?

198
00:10:22,710 --> 00:10:24,558
Yeah, sure.

199
00:10:25,292 --> 00:10:26,632
Follow me.

200
00:10:31,757 --> 00:10:33,323
Hey.

201
00:10:33,323 --> 00:10:34,396
What was that about?

202
00:10:34,396 --> 00:10:36,856
Why are we putting her on hold?

203
00:10:36,856 --> 00:10:41,396
Don't tell me you're actually
considering pimping her!

204
00:10:41,396 --> 00:10:43,260
She's pretty, sure, but that's...

205
00:10:43,260 --> 00:10:46,122
That's just wrong! She's a high schooler! Hey!

206
00:10:56,043 --> 00:11:01,636
[Dul Hee: Sam Hee, do you know
Sung Sae Ryeong from Upo High?]

207
00:11:01,636 --> 00:11:05,847
[Sure I do. She's Yu Gyeom's girlfriend.]

208
00:11:54,870 --> 00:11:57,323
You can drop me off over there.

209
00:12:06,289 --> 00:12:09,540
I'm sorry for that.

210
00:12:09,540 --> 00:12:11,840
I was on my phone.

211
00:12:12,690 --> 00:12:16,576
And, well... about the tutoring, you know...

212
00:12:16,576 --> 00:12:18,714
I'm not really experienced,

213
00:12:18,714 --> 00:12:23,202
and you can learn sign language
by watching videos at home.

214
00:12:23,202 --> 00:12:26,004
There's really no need for lessons.

215
00:12:27,456 --> 00:12:29,977
I thought I could just memorize it, too.

216
00:12:31,919 --> 00:12:34,379
But it's too fast.

217
00:12:34,379 --> 00:12:35,802
I can't follow.

218
00:12:37,016 --> 00:12:40,171
Well, you should ask them to slow down for you.

219
00:12:40,171 --> 00:12:42,544
I want to understand it all.

220
00:12:42,544 --> 00:12:44,656
But none of the videos I found

221
00:12:44,656 --> 00:12:47,303
showed anyone using sign language that fast.

222
00:12:47,303 --> 00:12:48,369
Well, yeah.

223
00:12:48,369 --> 00:12:51,974
I just think that's how teaching works.

224
00:12:51,974 --> 00:12:53,511
Just ask the other person to...

225
00:12:53,511 --> 00:12:55,767
But you were fast enough.

226
00:12:57,063 --> 00:12:59,002
- Me?
- Yes, you.

227
00:13:00,822 --> 00:13:03,353
Don't think too hard about it.

228
00:13:05,368 --> 00:13:10,749
Just talk to me in sign language,
and I'll try to understand you.

229
00:13:10,749 --> 00:13:12,014
That's all.

230
00:13:12,014 --> 00:13:13,100
And...

231
00:13:13,100 --> 00:13:16,000
There's no need to slow down for me.

232
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:18,274
I don't want you to teach me, either.

233
00:13:18,274 --> 00:13:20,574
Just make conversation with me.

234
00:13:20,574 --> 00:13:24,265
In time, I believe I'll get used to it.

235
00:13:27,940 --> 00:13:32,934
If it's the tutoring part that scares you,
we can be friends.

236
00:13:32,934 --> 00:13:36,553
- Just use sign language with me, and--
- I'd like to be friends!

237
00:13:41,047 --> 00:13:42,444
"Can do."

238
00:13:43,374 --> 00:13:44,759
"Not hard?"

239
00:13:47,114 --> 00:13:49,001
Yeah, friends.

240
00:13:50,874 --> 00:13:52,107
Thanks.

241
00:13:54,980 --> 00:13:56,387
I'll see you tomorrow if possible.

242
00:13:56,387 --> 00:13:57,839
I'll be in touch.

243
00:14:11,810 --> 00:14:13,340
I need to go.

244
00:14:16,856 --> 00:14:18,420
[Upo-ri Police Substation]

245
00:14:26,115 --> 00:14:29,883
I-I don't understand!

246
00:14:31,370 --> 00:14:32,907
Ma'am.

247
00:14:32,907 --> 00:14:34,327
Could you write it down for us?

248
00:14:34,327 --> 00:14:37,668
I'm sorry, but no one here knows sign language.

249
00:14:37,668 --> 00:14:39,504
I don't know!

250
00:14:39,504 --> 00:14:41,089
I don't understand what you're saying!

251
00:14:41,089 --> 00:14:42,958
This is driving me mad!

252
00:14:42,958 --> 00:14:44,708
- Sir.
- What do we do?

253
00:14:44,708 --> 00:14:46,912
Should we see if there are
any interpreters in town?

254
00:14:46,912 --> 00:14:48,262
Or we could call 110...

255
00:14:48,262 --> 00:14:49,939
Yes, yes!

256
00:14:51,887 --> 00:14:53,726
J-Just a minute, please!

257
00:14:53,726 --> 00:14:54,807
Oh my.

258
00:14:54,807 --> 00:14:56,294
Madam!

259
00:14:56,294 --> 00:14:57,908
Is something the matter?

260
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:02,108
Hello to you too.

261
00:15:05,822 --> 00:15:06,990
"Gone?"

262
00:15:06,990 --> 00:15:08,696
Who's gone?

263
00:15:09,527 --> 00:15:10,615
Who?

264
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:13,109
Sae Ryeong?

265
00:15:16,291 --> 00:15:18,640
Are you feeling ill, Jin Mi?

266
00:15:20,767 --> 00:15:22,837
Hey, Jin Mi...

267
00:15:25,886 --> 00:15:28,745
Come on, stop crying.

268
00:15:28,745 --> 00:15:31,658
Yeah, cut it out already.

269
00:15:34,360 --> 00:15:37,427
Come on, Jin Mi, talk to me.

270
00:15:42,460 --> 00:15:45,499
Jin Mi cried the whole day.

271
00:15:49,927 --> 00:15:53,115
She kept her head down
through every class since yesterday.

272
00:15:57,930 --> 00:16:01,997
She neither eats nor goes to the restroom.

273
00:16:01,997 --> 00:16:03,119
Ha Yeon.

274
00:16:04,637 --> 00:16:07,814
Do you think I'm in the wrong here?

275
00:16:11,530 --> 00:16:12,739
No.

276
00:16:14,237 --> 00:16:16,282
But you did go too far.

277
00:16:18,686 --> 00:16:22,370
She shouldn't have done that to me,

278
00:16:22,370 --> 00:16:24,397
but you shouldn't have
done that to her, either.

279
00:16:28,497 --> 00:16:32,302
I... get angry, sometimes.

280
00:16:37,023 --> 00:16:39,834
<i>I don't want to be here, either.</i>

281
00:16:39,834 --> 00:16:42,063
<i>We have no other choice. Let's go back inside.</i>

282
00:16:42,063 --> 00:16:44,296
<i>Hey! Babe!</i>

283
00:16:44,296 --> 00:16:46,100
<i>Damn!</i>

284
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:48,104
<i>I told you not to swear!</i>

285
00:16:48,104 --> 00:16:49,464
<i>I'm leaving.</i>

286
00:16:49,464 --> 00:16:51,087
<i>I'd rather die than live like Mom!</i>

287
00:16:51,087 --> 00:16:52,293
<i>Is that what you call living?</i>

288
00:16:52,293 --> 00:16:54,608
<i>You have no damn pride or self-respect!</i>

289
00:16:56,225 --> 00:16:58,531
<i>What are you doing?</i>

290
00:17:00,733 --> 00:17:04,184
<i>You need to calm down! What's wrong with you?</i>

291
00:17:04,184 --> 00:17:05,601
<i>Let her go.</i>

292
00:17:05,601 --> 00:17:10,118
<i>A beautiful, comfy garden is no use
if the flower doesn't want to be there.</i>

293
00:17:14,347 --> 00:17:16,526
<i>Just let her leave!</i>

294
00:17:24,120 --> 00:17:25,336
<i>Dul Hee...</i>

295
00:17:26,560 --> 00:17:27,861
<i>Dul Hee!</i>

296
00:17:29,047 --> 00:17:30,867
<i>Sister...</i>

297
00:17:30,867 --> 00:17:33,507
I guess it's an insecurity of mine.

298
00:17:33,507 --> 00:17:35,184
Whenever my belief that I've been

299
00:17:35,184 --> 00:17:38,200
doing well to protect something
so very dear to me...

300
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:40,396
gets proven otherwise...

301
00:17:42,040 --> 00:17:44,653
Whenever I find out that I...

302
00:17:44,653 --> 00:17:47,602
never had the power
to protect anything in the first place.

303
00:17:49,027 --> 00:17:50,224
No.

304
00:17:51,083 --> 00:17:53,917
You protected me well enough.

305
00:17:53,917 --> 00:17:56,579
You had the power to do so. I mean it.

306
00:17:58,717 --> 00:17:59,858
Alright.

307
00:18:02,283 --> 00:18:04,457
I'll apologize.

308
00:18:04,457 --> 00:18:05,845
Really?

309
00:18:06,883 --> 00:18:09,893
I've never done it before, but...

310
00:18:11,457 --> 00:18:14,563
You really are going to apologize to Jin Mi?

311
00:18:14,563 --> 00:18:15,923
I will. You were right.

312
00:18:15,923 --> 00:18:17,610
I went too far.

313
00:18:17,610 --> 00:18:19,453
I'll try apologizing.

314
00:18:19,453 --> 00:18:21,737
Wow.

315
00:18:21,737 --> 00:18:24,357
Does that make you happy?

316
00:18:24,357 --> 00:18:26,517
Yes, it does.

317
00:18:26,517 --> 00:18:28,225
I don't see why.

318
00:18:30,863 --> 00:18:34,894
Well, in movies, a cool male lead

319
00:18:34,894 --> 00:18:40,361
sometimes does things he'd never do
for an ordinary female lead.

320
00:18:41,371 --> 00:18:43,397
For example,

321
00:18:43,397 --> 00:18:47,596
a guy who never drives
suddenly starts driving for the girl.

322
00:18:47,596 --> 00:18:49,563
Stuff like that.

323
00:18:49,563 --> 00:18:52,183
You know what I thought when I saw that?

324
00:18:55,869 --> 00:18:57,794
That makes no damn sense at all.

325
00:18:59,997 --> 00:19:02,414
That man is so stunning.

326
00:19:02,414 --> 00:19:08,397
Why would he change himself
for such an insignificant woman?

327
00:19:10,050 --> 00:19:12,470
It just isn't realistic at all.

328
00:19:13,917 --> 00:19:18,700
Maybe that woman wasn't insignificant at all.

329
00:19:22,196 --> 00:19:23,566
You're right.

330
00:19:24,457 --> 00:19:28,880
That's exactly how you made me feel just now.

331
00:19:36,237 --> 00:19:38,748
I thought I was like a kettle.

332
00:19:41,430 --> 00:19:43,659
Like some faded curtains,

333
00:19:45,017 --> 00:19:48,169
or an old clock that no one looks at.

334
00:19:52,063 --> 00:19:54,954
But ever since I met you here...

335
00:19:55,950 --> 00:19:58,970
I feel like I'm the protagonist of a movie.

336
00:19:58,970 --> 00:20:00,396
All thanks to you.

337
00:20:02,050 --> 00:20:03,563
It's an honor.

338
00:20:03,563 --> 00:20:05,214
If I'm being honest,

339
00:20:05,214 --> 00:20:09,663
I never even felt like the protagonist
of my own life.

340
00:20:09,663 --> 00:20:14,270
Even my name is plain. I've had
several classmates with the same name.

341
00:20:15,464 --> 00:20:17,072
I beg to differ.

342
00:20:19,337 --> 00:20:20,521
What do you mean?

343
00:20:21,163 --> 00:20:23,283
Kim Ha Yeon. Your name.

344
00:20:23,283 --> 00:20:25,092
You're the first Ha Yeon I've ever met.

345
00:20:27,043 --> 00:20:30,463
Everything about you is a first for me.

346
00:20:41,543 --> 00:20:44,710
We only have two weeks left.

347
00:20:44,710 --> 00:20:45,855
Of what?

348
00:20:46,530 --> 00:20:47,984
Summer vacation.

349
00:20:52,803 --> 00:20:55,207
Mom! I finished up over there.
What should I do now?

350
00:20:55,207 --> 00:20:56,710
You can give me anything to do.

351
00:20:56,710 --> 00:21:00,230
I've got plenty of time
before I go play Korean chess with grandpa.

352
00:21:00,230 --> 00:21:01,550
It's alright.

353
00:21:01,550 --> 00:21:03,563
I've just finished up, too.

354
00:21:05,530 --> 00:21:07,350
What's going on?

355
00:21:07,350 --> 00:21:09,686
You seem excited.

356
00:21:09,686 --> 00:21:11,605
No, it's nothing.

357
00:21:11,605 --> 00:21:13,439
Sam Hee, did you hear?

358
00:21:13,439 --> 00:21:17,376
Sae Ryeong ran away.

359
00:21:18,010 --> 00:21:21,194
I found out when I stopped by the precinct
to drop off some beverages.

360
00:21:21,194 --> 00:21:24,402
Her grandmother was there to file a report.

361
00:21:25,270 --> 00:21:26,394
The police...

362
00:21:26,394 --> 00:21:30,493
They said they couldn't do
anything if she left on her own.

363
00:21:31,990 --> 00:21:34,314
But she's so young, I'm worried.

364
00:21:34,314 --> 00:21:35,837
So...

365
00:21:35,837 --> 00:21:37,050
Well...

366
00:21:37,050 --> 00:21:38,881
- Mom?
- Yes?

367
00:21:38,881 --> 00:21:40,056
What is it?

368
00:21:40,870 --> 00:21:42,095
It's just...

369
00:21:43,603 --> 00:21:45,488
Sister asked me about Sae Ryeong.

370
00:21:48,237 --> 00:21:49,821
Who? What?

371
00:21:51,230 --> 00:21:52,315
My sister.

372
00:21:55,783 --> 00:21:57,201
Do you mean...

373
00:21:57,907 --> 00:21:59,846
Cho Dul Hee?

374
00:22:08,880 --> 00:22:10,727
Are you keeping in contact with her?

375
00:22:10,727 --> 00:22:12,917
No, I mean, sometimes. Rarely.

376
00:22:12,917 --> 00:22:14,780
Cho Sam Hee.

377
00:22:14,780 --> 00:22:17,044
She left this house.

378
00:22:17,800 --> 00:22:20,296
Why would you keep in touch
with someone like her?

379
00:22:22,747 --> 00:22:24,847
You're getting on my nerves.

380
00:22:31,292 --> 00:22:33,880
[ryu_siyeol]
[Karaoke Time After So Long!]

381
00:22:57,709 --> 00:22:58,899
Hey.

382
00:22:59,727 --> 00:23:01,012
Come outside.

383
00:23:13,080 --> 00:23:14,763
Hey.

384
00:23:14,763 --> 00:23:16,709
Sister here says she knows you.

385
00:23:18,903 --> 00:23:20,122
Me?

386
00:23:20,783 --> 00:23:22,383
You know me?

387
00:23:23,141 --> 00:23:25,014
How do you know me?

388
00:23:26,920 --> 00:23:28,904
She wants to know why you ran away.

389
00:23:28,904 --> 00:23:31,468
I want to know how she knows me.

390
00:23:31,468 --> 00:23:32,520
Hey.

391
00:23:32,520 --> 00:23:34,292
Answer the question. Why did you run away?

392
00:23:34,292 --> 00:23:36,220
Tell me how she knows...

393
00:23:38,864 --> 00:23:40,984
Hey. Don't you know who I am?

394
00:23:44,580 --> 00:23:46,285
Cho Yu Gyeom?

395
00:23:46,285 --> 00:23:48,603
Just tell me already.

396
00:23:48,603 --> 00:23:51,261
Why did you leave home?

397
00:23:52,133 --> 00:23:54,564
I didn't expect to see
his second older sister here.

398
00:23:54,564 --> 00:23:55,727
Your name was...

399
00:23:55,727 --> 00:23:58,077
Dul Ja, or Dul Jae, or...

400
00:23:58,077 --> 00:23:59,718
It's Dul Hee.

401
00:23:59,718 --> 00:24:01,305
Right, Dul Hee.

402
00:24:01,305 --> 00:24:02,740
Cho Dul Hee.

403
00:24:02,740 --> 00:24:05,653
It's nice to see you.

404
00:24:05,653 --> 00:24:08,700
I'm asking why you left home!

405
00:24:08,700 --> 00:24:09,724
Why?

406
00:24:09,724 --> 00:24:11,529
To make money, of course.

407
00:24:11,529 --> 00:24:13,114
Your family is rich, aren't they?

408
00:24:31,060 --> 00:24:33,627
It was all a lie.

409
00:24:33,627 --> 00:24:35,442
I got caught, so I ran away.

410
00:24:35,442 --> 00:24:36,630
What?

411
00:24:36,630 --> 00:24:41,069
So I'm looking to make money fast and easy.

412
00:24:41,069 --> 00:24:43,393
A lot of it.

413
00:24:43,393 --> 00:24:46,412
We already told you that's
not how we do things here.

414
00:24:47,567 --> 00:24:49,293
Can't you just do it for me?

415
00:24:49,293 --> 00:24:51,772
As a favor between acquaintances.

416
00:24:51,772 --> 00:24:53,981
You have no status, and you're underage.

417
00:24:53,981 --> 00:24:56,427
If you want to make easy money, and fast...

418
00:24:59,206 --> 00:25:01,450
it's all illegal.

419
00:25:01,450 --> 00:25:03,873
And if you start working illegal jobs...

420
00:25:05,883 --> 00:25:10,337
Well, there's a big hospital
across the intersection there.

421
00:25:10,337 --> 00:25:11,923
That's where you'll end up.

422
00:25:11,923 --> 00:25:13,337
Well...

423
00:25:13,337 --> 00:25:15,813
The ICU or the morgue, probably.

424
00:25:16,470 --> 00:25:17,470
Why?

425
00:25:18,303 --> 00:25:21,301
Because your body will be ruined in no time.

426
00:25:21,301 --> 00:25:22,459
So--

427
00:25:22,459 --> 00:25:24,542
Go home right now.

428
00:25:29,393 --> 00:25:30,820
I don't want to.

429
00:25:31,891 --> 00:25:33,070
What's the matter?

430
00:25:33,070 --> 00:25:35,013
You ran away, too, right?

431
00:25:36,172 --> 00:25:37,474
You sure are one of a kind.

432
00:25:37,474 --> 00:25:40,360
Dul Hee, what's up with this girl anyway?

433
00:25:40,360 --> 00:25:42,130
I didn't say anything wrong.

434
00:25:42,130 --> 00:25:45,190
You left your home and ended up here.

435
00:25:45,190 --> 00:25:46,997
But look where we are.

436
00:25:46,997 --> 00:25:50,497
This isn't the ICU,
and it certainly isn't a morgue.

437
00:25:52,593 --> 00:25:57,804
I heard Yu Gyeom searched
like a madman to find you,

438
00:25:57,804 --> 00:25:59,789
and when he did, you told him this.

439
00:25:59,789 --> 00:26:02,201
"Fuck off, you bastard!"

440
00:26:03,273 --> 00:26:06,333
You're a true hypocrite, aren't you?

441
00:26:06,333 --> 00:26:08,647
You remind me of Yu Gyeom.

442
00:26:08,647 --> 00:26:11,260
Does it run in your family or something?

443
00:26:11,260 --> 00:26:12,793
Who are you to say that?

444
00:26:12,793 --> 00:26:14,447
Who do you think you are?

445
00:26:14,447 --> 00:26:19,046
So you can't tell me what to do.

446
00:26:28,660 --> 00:26:30,280
By the way...

447
00:26:30,280 --> 00:26:33,540
I get that you won't let teenagers
do anything illegal.

448
00:26:33,540 --> 00:26:34,722
But...

449
00:26:36,920 --> 00:26:39,718
I guess different rules apply to adults.

450
00:26:40,683 --> 00:26:46,070
I mean, the room that you
put me in reeks of weed.

451
00:26:46,070 --> 00:26:48,543
I'm guessing you smoke weed here?

452
00:26:48,543 --> 00:26:52,410
And I've seen the women here.
They obviously work in dubious places.

453
00:26:52,410 --> 00:26:57,309
I don't know if you know,
but I'm very good at filing police reports.

454
00:27:06,458 --> 00:27:07,586
Yu Gyeom!

455
00:27:07,586 --> 00:27:09,893
- Leave me alone.
- Yu Gyeom!

456
00:27:10,797 --> 00:27:12,020
Come on!

457
00:27:13,109 --> 00:27:14,801
Listen.

458
00:27:14,801 --> 00:27:17,219
- I just...
- What is it?

459
00:27:17,971 --> 00:27:19,848
No, it's just that...

460
00:27:19,848 --> 00:27:21,309
Come with me.

461
00:27:22,337 --> 00:27:23,356
Hurry!

462
00:27:25,145 --> 00:27:26,574
Um...

463
00:27:26,574 --> 00:27:28,619
Did Sae Ryeong run away from home?

464
00:27:29,930 --> 00:27:33,612
I was just wondering if she went to Seoul.

465
00:27:33,612 --> 00:27:35,143
How would I know?

466
00:27:35,143 --> 00:27:36,330
Why not?

467
00:27:36,330 --> 00:27:38,532
Because we broke up.

468
00:27:38,532 --> 00:27:41,177
Why? Why on earth did you break up?

469
00:27:41,177 --> 00:27:43,506
Is this what you wanted me for?

470
00:27:44,203 --> 00:27:45,707
We broke up.

471
00:27:45,707 --> 00:27:46,951
And I don't care about her.

472
00:27:46,951 --> 00:27:47,983
Is that clear?

473
00:27:47,983 --> 00:27:50,416
Wait, Dul Hee texted me.

474
00:27:53,298 --> 00:27:56,260
Sae Ryeong is there with her.

475
00:27:56,260 --> 00:27:57,644
With Dul Hee.

476
00:27:58,824 --> 00:28:00,940
She wants to prostitute herself.

477
00:28:03,003 --> 00:28:04,557
What?

478
00:28:04,557 --> 00:28:07,104
[Are you deaf? Are you hard of hearing?]
I'm telling you!

479
00:28:07,104 --> 00:28:09,648
She's been acting so weird lately!

480
00:28:10,649 --> 00:28:14,477
Where the hell is she now?

481
00:28:14,477 --> 00:28:17,167
She keeps going out at night!

482
00:28:17,167 --> 00:28:19,158
It's keeping me up all night!

483
00:28:19,158 --> 00:28:20,490
Kim Ha Yeon!

484
00:28:20,490 --> 00:28:21,950
Hey, Kim Ha Yeon!

485
00:28:23,710 --> 00:28:24,808
What the...

486
00:28:25,747 --> 00:28:27,117
You...

487
00:28:27,117 --> 00:28:29,027
Were you here all this time?

488
00:28:29,027 --> 00:28:30,120
Yes.

489
00:28:32,610 --> 00:28:35,211
Were you studying?

490
00:28:36,443 --> 00:28:38,087
- Yes.
- See?

491
00:28:38,087 --> 00:28:40,271
I told you you were being hysterical.

492
00:28:40,271 --> 00:28:42,189
Keep at it, Ha Yeon.

493
00:28:42,189 --> 00:28:43,781
Come on, leave her alone.

494
00:28:48,150 --> 00:28:51,121
You should get off her back.
You'll only stress her out.

495
00:28:54,630 --> 00:28:57,570
You never pay attention to the kids.

496
00:28:57,570 --> 00:28:59,825
I have my reasons, you know!

497
00:29:02,297 --> 00:29:03,583
Hey.

498
00:29:03,583 --> 00:29:05,763
What are you snickering at?

499
00:29:05,763 --> 00:29:06,763
What?

500
00:29:08,310 --> 00:29:09,450
Nothing.

501
00:29:09,450 --> 00:29:10,837
It's nothing.

502
00:29:10,837 --> 00:29:14,179
I'm just so touchy these days.

503
00:29:14,179 --> 00:29:15,953
Really, I just can't...

504
00:29:18,227 --> 00:29:19,328
Mom?

505
00:29:20,330 --> 00:29:22,648
May I buy a game pack?

506
00:29:22,648 --> 00:29:23,959
Sure.

507
00:29:23,959 --> 00:29:25,291
How much is it?

508
00:29:27,330 --> 00:29:28,337
300,000 won.

509
00:29:28,337 --> 00:29:31,049
[Transfer to: Noh Dae Hyeon]
[Confirm]

510
00:29:31,049 --> 00:29:32,340
[Please confirm the recipient's name]
[Noh Dae Hyeon]

511
00:29:32,340 --> 00:29:36,170
[Transfer 300,000 won to Noh Dae Hyeon]
No one in this house ever stands up for me!

512
00:29:36,170 --> 00:29:37,982
I'm the only one who cares.

513
00:29:39,583 --> 00:29:42,779
Come on, talk to me, Jin Mi.

514
00:29:42,779 --> 00:29:46,470
How would I know what's wrong
if you won't talk to me?

515
00:29:46,470 --> 00:29:49,277
What happened to you?

516
00:29:49,277 --> 00:29:51,787
It's been days now!

517
00:29:51,787 --> 00:29:53,292
Leave her alone.

518
00:29:53,292 --> 00:29:54,554
She must be on her period.

519
00:29:54,554 --> 00:29:55,911
Hey, you. She's not.

520
00:29:55,911 --> 00:29:57,430
"Hey, yew, she's nawt."

521
00:29:57,430 --> 00:29:58,561
Hey, hey!

522
00:29:58,561 --> 00:30:00,917
Surely you must know why she's doing this.

523
00:30:00,917 --> 00:30:02,901
What's up with her?

524
00:30:04,710 --> 00:30:08,034
Please, Jin Mi! Please!

525
00:30:08,034 --> 00:30:09,058
Lee Won Bae.

526
00:30:09,058 --> 00:30:10,382
Are you sure you didn't do something wrong?

527
00:30:10,382 --> 00:30:15,126
No! We haven't even seen each other recently,
so how could I have done anything wrong?

528
00:30:15,126 --> 00:30:17,681
If... If I...

529
00:30:17,681 --> 00:30:20,378
If I did anything wrong,
I guess it was just existing!

530
00:30:20,378 --> 00:30:22,603
- Satisfied?
- What?

531
00:30:22,603 --> 00:30:24,420
So riled up.

532
00:30:25,170 --> 00:30:26,361
Yu Gyeom's here.

533
00:30:26,361 --> 00:30:27,430
Cho Yu Gyeom!

534
00:30:27,430 --> 00:30:29,187
Why, why?

535
00:30:29,187 --> 00:30:30,971
Why won't you talk to me?

536
00:30:30,971 --> 00:30:35,657
Why, why, why?

537
00:30:35,657 --> 00:30:36,681
Hey, Kim Jin Mi.

538
00:30:36,681 --> 00:30:39,031
- Why.
- Cho Yu Gyeom wants to see you.

539
00:30:53,483 --> 00:30:55,449
For the phone that I broke.

540
00:30:55,449 --> 00:30:57,643
I-I'm sorry.

541
00:31:00,310 --> 00:31:01,457
I'm sorry.

542
00:31:01,457 --> 00:31:03,897
I went too far.

543
00:31:03,897 --> 00:31:07,791
I'm sorry for yelling and
taking my anger out on you.

544
00:31:08,958 --> 00:31:11,357
I'm sorry. I mean it.

545
00:31:11,357 --> 00:31:13,610
No, it's fine.

546
00:31:13,610 --> 00:31:15,879
Thank you for accepting my apology.

547
00:31:16,930 --> 00:31:18,897
It's nothing...

548
00:31:18,897 --> 00:31:21,659
But I think you should apologize too,
when you get the chance.

549
00:31:22,923 --> 00:31:24,217
Right.

550
00:31:24,217 --> 00:31:25,921
I'm sorry to you, too, for--

551
00:31:25,921 --> 00:31:27,503
No, not to me.

552
00:31:27,503 --> 00:31:29,128
To Kim Ha Yeon.

553
00:31:29,128 --> 00:31:30,216
Kim Ha Yeon?

554
00:31:30,216 --> 00:31:32,775
You dumped dirty water on her.

555
00:31:34,397 --> 00:31:35,737
Right, right.

556
00:31:35,737 --> 00:31:37,768
I'll apologize.

557
00:31:40,130 --> 00:31:42,160
Do you want me to do it now?

558
00:31:42,160 --> 00:31:44,199
Yeah, that would be best.

559
00:31:45,177 --> 00:31:46,548
Okay.

560
00:31:49,446 --> 00:31:51,057
Wait, I-I'll go out right now.

561
00:31:51,057 --> 00:31:52,494
Excuse me, just wait.

562
00:31:52,494 --> 00:31:53,745
Hey, you! What was that?

563
00:31:53,745 --> 00:31:56,577
Why are you giving her a whole new phone?

564
00:31:56,577 --> 00:31:58,797
I smashed her phone to bits.

565
00:32:06,450 --> 00:32:07,828
I'm...

566
00:32:11,763 --> 00:32:13,025
Well...

567
00:32:15,923 --> 00:32:16,947
Yeah.

568
00:32:16,947 --> 00:32:18,182
You can say it.

569
00:32:18,907 --> 00:32:21,670
About that time I dumped dirty water on you...

570
00:32:21,670 --> 00:32:23,363
I'm sorry.

571
00:32:23,363 --> 00:32:24,710
I really am.

572
00:32:26,303 --> 00:32:27,721
It's okay.

573
00:32:31,043 --> 00:32:32,573
It's fine.

574
00:32:33,550 --> 00:32:35,584
Thank you for apologizing.

575
00:32:38,063 --> 00:32:39,268
Me too.

576
00:32:44,037 --> 00:32:45,452
Hey, Kim Jin Mi.

577
00:32:46,310 --> 00:32:48,043
Come back out here for a second.

578
00:32:48,043 --> 00:32:49,463
Me?

579
00:32:49,463 --> 00:32:50,716
Again?

580
00:32:58,014 --> 00:32:59,060
T-This is...

581
00:32:59,060 --> 00:33:01,064
I'm not angry. I just want to know.

582
00:33:02,223 --> 00:33:04,318
Can you tell me...

583
00:33:04,318 --> 00:33:06,399
what's going on here?

584
00:33:16,411 --> 00:33:18,903
<i>Sae Ryeong's place of residence...</i>

585
00:33:18,903 --> 00:33:20,593
<i>was all a lie.</i>

586
00:33:21,683 --> 00:33:24,299
<i>Turns out, it was some
lawmaker's vacation home.</i>

587
00:33:25,756 --> 00:33:28,696
<i>You know, right? My dad's a lawmaker.</i>

588
00:33:28,696 --> 00:33:30,410
<i>A three-term lawmaker.</i>

589
00:33:30,410 --> 00:33:31,847
<i>Obviously...</i>

590
00:33:31,847 --> 00:33:35,817
<i>the owner of that house isn't Sae Ryeong's dad.</i>

591
00:33:35,817 --> 00:33:38,630
<i>She worked there and gained access that way.</i>

592
00:33:38,630 --> 00:33:40,737
<i>You should go now, Yu Gyeom.</i>

593
00:33:40,737 --> 00:33:42,397
<i>You head inside first.</i>

594
00:33:42,397 --> 00:33:44,023
<i>No, you go home first.</i>

595
00:33:44,023 --> 00:33:45,347
<i>No, you go ahead.</i>

596
00:33:45,347 --> 00:33:46,751
<i>Come on, you go ahead.</i>

597
00:33:46,751 --> 00:33:49,037
<i>- No, I'm fine.
- Hurry up and go home.</i>

598
00:33:49,037 --> 00:33:50,100
<i>Go on.</i>

599
00:33:50,983 --> 00:33:52,170
<i>Okay, then.</i>

600
00:33:52,170 --> 00:33:53,421
<i>- I'll get going.
- Okay.</i>

601
00:33:53,421 --> 00:33:55,125
<i>- She's poor in reality,
- Bye.</i>

602
00:33:55,125 --> 00:33:57,402
but pretended to be well-off.

603
00:34:03,750 --> 00:34:05,377
What the hell.

604
00:34:05,377 --> 00:34:07,137
Hey, did you see the thing?

605
00:34:07,137 --> 00:34:09,017
God damn it.

606
00:34:09,017 --> 00:34:12,343
She sure is a whole new type of crazy.

607
00:34:12,343 --> 00:34:13,390
What?

608
00:34:15,399 --> 00:34:16,832
Sung Sae Ryeong?

609
00:34:39,037 --> 00:34:40,567
You're here early.

610
00:34:43,770 --> 00:34:44,783
I am.

611
00:34:50,043 --> 00:34:51,768
Do you like rainy days?

612
00:34:51,768 --> 00:34:52,768
I do.

613
00:34:54,062 --> 00:34:55,615
"I do."

614
00:34:56,597 --> 00:34:59,390
Why? Do you not like the rain?

615
00:34:59,390 --> 00:35:00,485
Right.

616
00:35:00,485 --> 00:35:02,013
"Why? Do you not like the rain?"

617
00:35:02,690 --> 00:35:04,787
Don't most people?

618
00:35:05,817 --> 00:35:08,550
Everyone likes sunny days.

619
00:35:08,550 --> 00:35:10,080
Clear, sunny days.

620
00:35:10,787 --> 00:35:12,900
I like it.

621
00:35:16,670 --> 00:35:21,190
Clear days, rainy days, cloudy days.

622
00:35:30,817 --> 00:35:32,970
<i>I like...</i>

623
00:35:32,970 --> 00:35:34,340
<i>all of them.</i>

624
00:35:55,223 --> 00:35:57,306
Would you rather I only use sign language?

625
00:36:02,290 --> 00:36:03,720
Let's go eat something.

626
00:36:04,517 --> 00:36:05,810
What do you want to eat?

627
00:36:05,810 --> 00:36:07,144
Anything's fine.

628
00:36:19,097 --> 00:36:20,667
You should've said something.

629
00:36:20,667 --> 00:36:22,672
What foods do you like?

630
00:36:24,383 --> 00:36:25,590
That was too fast for me.

631
00:36:25,590 --> 00:36:27,689
I said, "What foods do you like?"

632
00:36:28,723 --> 00:36:30,132
I'm not picky.

633
00:36:31,491 --> 00:36:32,869
I see.

634
00:36:34,786 --> 00:36:36,163
What the hell is this?

635
00:36:36,163 --> 00:36:37,597
What do you mean?

636
00:36:37,597 --> 00:36:38,687
It's a karaoke place.

637
00:36:38,687 --> 00:36:40,070
Well, yes, so...

638
00:36:40,070 --> 00:36:41,681
So what am I supposed to do here?

639
00:36:41,681 --> 00:36:43,958
You'll be working reception, okay?

640
00:36:43,958 --> 00:36:47,379
Luckily for you, the owner offered good pay.

641
00:36:47,379 --> 00:36:48,448
Now...

642
00:36:49,163 --> 00:36:51,224
What do you mean, I'll be a receptionist?

643
00:36:51,224 --> 00:36:52,345
Hey.

644
00:36:52,345 --> 00:36:55,338
Didn't I tell you that I want
to make a lot of money?

645
00:36:55,338 --> 00:36:57,202
So what's all this about
working as a receptionist?

646
00:36:58,061 --> 00:36:59,855
You know...

647
00:36:59,855 --> 00:37:03,139
I can do other things, if you catch my drift.

648
00:37:03,139 --> 00:37:05,676
I want to work somewhere more...

649
00:37:05,676 --> 00:37:07,267
You know what I mean!

650
00:37:07,267 --> 00:37:08,460
Hey!

651
00:37:12,061 --> 00:37:13,808
You're eighteen years old.

652
00:37:13,808 --> 00:37:16,245
Eighteen, you weenie!

653
00:37:16,245 --> 00:37:19,535
If you want to sell your body that much,
don't come asking us for work.

654
00:37:19,535 --> 00:37:24,010
If you really want to make money,
go back to school and graduate first.

655
00:37:24,010 --> 00:37:26,754
You can then get hired by a company
that'll pay you well!

656
00:37:26,754 --> 00:37:28,251
You're such a...

657
00:37:28,251 --> 00:37:30,978
You must be out of your mind
if prostitution is your dream job!

658
00:37:30,978 --> 00:37:33,151
That's not something to dream about.

659
00:37:34,545 --> 00:37:36,058
Hey.

660
00:37:36,058 --> 00:37:38,962
This job is the best-paying one we got today.

661
00:37:38,962 --> 00:37:41,185
So shut it and work the front desk.

662
00:37:41,185 --> 00:37:43,755
Don't forget to give an extra 30 minutes
to all the customers.

663
00:37:59,151 --> 00:38:00,778
What's wrong with you?

664
00:38:05,271 --> 00:38:06,987
I can't stand to watch.

665
00:38:09,445 --> 00:38:12,531
You know where Sae Ryeong is, right?

666
00:38:12,531 --> 00:38:14,061
Yeah, I do.

667
00:38:14,844 --> 00:38:17,145
Then can't we just go get her?

668
00:38:17,145 --> 00:38:18,532
We can't.

669
00:38:20,931 --> 00:38:23,569
Then we should go tell her grandma.

670
00:38:23,569 --> 00:38:26,913
We'll tell her that Sae Ryeong is okay,
and give her your sister's number.

671
00:38:26,913 --> 00:38:29,131
We can do that, right?

672
00:38:29,131 --> 00:38:30,981
Sure. Let's do that.

673
00:38:35,114 --> 00:38:40,182
But she can't talk, can't hear,
and I doubt she can text.

674
00:38:43,551 --> 00:38:46,475
What if I call your sister and relay it to--

675
00:38:46,475 --> 00:38:47,806
Ha Yeon.

676
00:38:50,518 --> 00:38:52,142
Does it bother you that much?

677
00:38:56,292 --> 00:38:58,056
Sorry.

678
00:38:58,056 --> 00:39:00,865
I just have no tolerance for these things.

679
00:39:01,765 --> 00:39:04,164
For all things pitiful.

680
00:39:04,164 --> 00:39:05,789
Why not?

681
00:39:09,971 --> 00:39:11,638
I see myself in them.

682
00:39:12,863 --> 00:39:16,529
I can't just walk past someone
carrying heavy loads all alone,

683
00:39:17,505 --> 00:39:21,085
or someone being ignored.

684
00:39:21,085 --> 00:39:24,896
I can't sit by and watch someone cry
at their desk all day.

685
00:39:27,198 --> 00:39:29,648
I see myself in all of them.

686
00:39:35,552 --> 00:39:37,638
I've...

687
00:39:37,638 --> 00:39:40,929
never been to Seoul, except for
that time I went to look for you.

688
00:39:42,881 --> 00:39:45,435
I'm not saying
we should go find Sung Sae Ryeong,

689
00:39:45,435 --> 00:39:47,549
or go visit my sister.

690
00:39:49,068 --> 00:39:50,515
What I'm saying is...

691
00:39:52,521 --> 00:39:54,152
I'll be going on a trip to Seoul with you.

692
00:39:54,152 --> 00:39:55,420
For the first time ever.

693
00:40:00,948 --> 00:40:01,985
Let's go now.

694
00:40:01,985 --> 00:40:03,295
To Seoul.

695
00:40:28,268 --> 00:40:30,355
How dare you!

696
00:40:31,068 --> 00:40:32,507
Did you just hit me?

697
00:40:34,055 --> 00:40:35,632
You touched me.

698
00:40:35,632 --> 00:40:38,123
Now I want to get paid. What's wrong with that?

699
00:40:38,123 --> 00:40:39,447
Wow, really...

700
00:40:39,447 --> 00:40:40,804
Where's the manager? Hey!

701
00:40:40,804 --> 00:40:42,455
I didn't request you.

702
00:40:42,455 --> 00:40:44,959
You're the one who barged in
and got all up in my face!

703
00:40:44,959 --> 00:40:47,355
And you have the audacity to ask me for money?

704
00:40:47,951 --> 00:40:49,902
You touched me anyway.

705
00:40:49,902 --> 00:40:52,911
- You fondled me!
- What's going on here?

706
00:40:52,911 --> 00:40:55,622
- What's the matter?
- I want the manager.

707
00:40:55,622 --> 00:40:57,472
This lunatic just let herself in and--

708
00:40:57,472 --> 00:40:58,709
Excuse me?

709
00:40:58,709 --> 00:41:00,005
She did what?

710
00:41:01,101 --> 00:41:02,691
Seriously.

711
00:41:02,691 --> 00:41:04,221
I'm sorry about that.

712
00:41:04,964 --> 00:41:06,175
No, I'll go.

713
00:41:06,175 --> 00:41:07,585
I'll go right away.

714
00:41:07,585 --> 00:41:08,895
Okay.

715
00:41:11,137 --> 00:41:12,422
Dul Hee!

716
00:41:13,606 --> 00:41:14,764
What?

717
00:41:14,764 --> 00:41:17,717
That Sung Sae Ryeong kid
is not right in the head!

718
00:41:18,817 --> 00:41:19,970
Ha Yeon.

719
00:41:21,551 --> 00:41:23,104
Yes?

720
00:41:23,104 --> 00:41:25,130
I want to ask you something.

721
00:41:33,368 --> 00:41:35,228
No, I don't want to!

722
00:41:35,228 --> 00:41:36,252
Hey!

723
00:41:36,252 --> 00:41:37,677
I should...

724
00:41:40,364 --> 00:41:41,612
You.

725
00:41:41,612 --> 00:41:43,819
Head back to your room.

726
00:41:43,819 --> 00:41:45,592
Now!

727
00:41:45,592 --> 00:41:46,725
Dul Hee.

728
00:41:46,725 --> 00:41:48,112
What should we do with her?

729
00:41:48,112 --> 00:41:49,749
We'll have to send her back.

730
00:41:49,749 --> 00:41:51,037
Is there anyone who can?

731
00:41:52,760 --> 00:41:54,066
Wait.

732
00:41:54,066 --> 00:41:55,651
I'll find someone.

733
00:41:57,351 --> 00:41:59,389
I should call your parents and...

734
00:42:00,539 --> 00:42:02,132
Right, you don't have parents.

735
00:42:02,132 --> 00:42:05,349
Whatever, surely someone will come get you.

736
00:42:05,349 --> 00:42:07,168
Go to your room and wait.

737
00:42:08,703 --> 00:42:10,885
Report us if you want. Go ahead!

738
00:42:10,885 --> 00:42:12,265
Screw it!

739
00:42:12,265 --> 00:42:13,981
I'll report you, too!

740
00:42:13,981 --> 00:42:15,212
Really!

741
00:42:15,212 --> 00:42:16,652
You're not like any other delinquent.

742
00:42:16,652 --> 00:42:18,716
You're truly something else!

743
00:42:21,555 --> 00:42:23,492
- What's up?
- Hey!

744
00:42:23,492 --> 00:42:26,319
Great timing.
Take her back to her room, will you?

745
00:42:26,319 --> 00:42:29,424
What? No, I'm busy. I can't.

746
00:42:32,385 --> 00:42:34,446
I guess I can.

747
00:42:35,232 --> 00:42:36,900
I'll just drop her off.

748
00:42:36,900 --> 00:42:37,915
Okay.

749
00:42:38,699 --> 00:42:40,239
Hey.

750
00:42:40,239 --> 00:42:42,279
She's underage.

751
00:42:42,279 --> 00:42:44,140
Don't even think about it.

752
00:43:29,922 --> 00:43:31,626
Hey, mister?

753
00:43:34,462 --> 00:43:36,535
Do you have any money?

754
00:43:36,535 --> 00:43:39,035
- What?
- Have you got money?

755
00:43:39,035 --> 00:43:40,595
To pay me with?

756
00:43:59,462 --> 00:44:02,433
What? That's disgusting.

757
00:44:04,705 --> 00:44:05,736
Come here.

758
00:44:05,736 --> 00:44:07,842
She's pretty.

759
00:44:07,842 --> 00:44:09,495
Cute girl.

760
00:44:13,489 --> 00:44:14,679
It's okay.

761
00:44:29,135 --> 00:44:31,613
- What?
- What? Go somewhere else!

762
00:44:31,613 --> 00:44:32,629
What?

763
00:44:32,629 --> 00:44:34,622
What did you say to us?

764
00:44:34,622 --> 00:44:36,406
- Hey, man!
- How dare you!

765
00:44:36,406 --> 00:44:39,617
- You're nothing!
- Go home if you're drunk!

766
00:44:41,605 --> 00:44:43,043
Die, you sly fox!

767
00:44:43,043 --> 00:44:44,259
- It hurts!
- What are you gawking at?

768
00:44:44,259 --> 00:44:45,283
Hey!

769
00:44:45,283 --> 00:44:47,656
- What're you looking at?
- Shut it!

770
00:44:47,656 --> 00:44:49,686
- It hurts!
- Be quiet!

771
00:44:49,686 --> 00:44:51,457
- I said I'm sorry!
- Same old, every day.

772
00:44:51,457 --> 00:44:53,580
Seriously, what's her issue?

773
00:44:57,820 --> 00:45:00,942
You bastard! What are you doing here?

774
00:45:00,942 --> 00:45:03,295
What's your problem?

775
00:45:03,295 --> 00:45:04,695
Excuse me...

776
00:45:05,589 --> 00:45:08,194
Why would you smack someone's head like that?

777
00:45:09,759 --> 00:45:12,070
Get lost, you piece of shit!

778
00:45:15,602 --> 00:45:16,833
That's your little brother?

779
00:45:16,833 --> 00:45:18,403
Why'd you hit me?

780
00:45:18,403 --> 00:45:21,007
Yu Gyeom, this place is bad.

781
00:45:21,007 --> 00:45:22,298
Let's report it to the police.

782
00:45:22,298 --> 00:45:25,909
Once we get Sae Ryeong back,
let's just call the police on this place.

783
00:45:25,909 --> 00:45:28,939
Is today National Report to
the Police Day or something?

784
00:45:28,939 --> 00:45:31,948
Yu Gyeom, people like these are lost causes.

785
00:45:31,948 --> 00:45:34,520
Violence is bad, right?

786
00:45:35,746 --> 00:45:37,962
Who's she?

787
00:45:37,962 --> 00:45:39,387
She's my girlfriend.

788
00:45:56,016 --> 00:45:58,119
Wasn't your girlfriend Sae Ryeong?

789
00:46:00,145 --> 00:46:02,937
Your girlfriend. I heard she's Sung Sae Ryeong.

790
00:46:02,937 --> 00:46:04,736
No.

791
00:46:05,615 --> 00:46:08,722
You're not even dating Sung Sae Ryeong,
so why are you here?

792
00:46:08,722 --> 00:46:10,767
I just wanted to see what Seoul's all about.

793
00:46:11,782 --> 00:46:14,358
Must be nice to have it so easy.

794
00:46:15,362 --> 00:46:16,995
So is that...

795
00:46:17,935 --> 00:46:19,555
your girlfriend?

796
00:46:19,555 --> 00:46:20,650
Yep.

797
00:46:25,418 --> 00:46:30,855
You two are a damn perfect match.

798
00:46:33,748 --> 00:46:38,779
So what if we're a damn perfect match?
It's my relationship.

799
00:46:38,779 --> 00:46:41,186
I'll date whoever I want.

800
00:46:41,186 --> 00:46:44,690
I just think you two are fucking ridiculous.

801
00:46:44,690 --> 00:46:47,391
What are you going to do about it?

802
00:46:50,668 --> 00:46:53,448
At least I don't stalk
people like you do, sister.

803
00:46:53,448 --> 00:46:56,842
Remember that medical student
who used to tutor you?

804
00:46:56,842 --> 00:47:00,911
You practically stalked him.

805
00:47:00,911 --> 00:47:04,193
Now that's fucking ridiculous.

806
00:47:07,682 --> 00:47:09,382
- Hey, miss.
- Yeah?

807
00:47:09,382 --> 00:47:11,898
What are they saying?

808
00:47:13,215 --> 00:47:15,134
Let's see...

809
00:47:15,134 --> 00:47:16,152
Do you want to die?

810
00:47:16,152 --> 00:47:17,839
"You crazy bastard,"

811
00:47:17,839 --> 00:47:21,309
something about dirty water...

812
00:47:21,309 --> 00:47:22,726
"You should..."

813
00:47:22,726 --> 00:47:24,955
"know your limits."

814
00:47:24,955 --> 00:47:28,195
Yada yada. Basically, you shouldn't be dating.

815
00:47:28,195 --> 00:47:29,285
What?

816
00:47:30,431 --> 00:47:32,561
Let's see...

817
00:47:32,561 --> 00:47:35,153
Your boyfriend says,

818
00:47:35,153 --> 00:47:36,977
"Mind your own business."

819
00:47:36,977 --> 00:47:38,789
"Screw you."

820
00:47:38,789 --> 00:47:41,149
And she says...

821
00:47:41,149 --> 00:47:43,462
"You little bastard," and...

822
00:47:43,462 --> 00:47:46,374
In conclusion, she doesn't want you to date.

823
00:47:48,109 --> 00:47:51,173
Then I'll swear in sign language, damn it!

824
00:47:51,173 --> 00:47:53,383
My vocal cords are stuck together.

825
00:47:53,383 --> 00:47:56,584
How else am I supposed to swear?

826
00:47:59,530 --> 00:48:02,830
You're really lowering yourself.

827
00:48:04,934 --> 00:48:06,215
Who said you could call me that?

828
00:48:06,215 --> 00:48:08,789
Do I even need to keep going?

829
00:48:08,789 --> 00:48:12,675
It's all just "you jerk, you bastard,
screw you, shut up," the full set.

830
00:48:12,675 --> 00:48:13,699
Miss.

831
00:48:13,699 --> 00:48:17,143
I thought sign language was graceful.

832
00:48:17,143 --> 00:48:18,535
Me too.

833
00:48:18,535 --> 00:48:21,220
I thought the same thing until I met her.

834
00:48:33,482 --> 00:48:35,570
You promise to pay me, right?

835
00:48:38,249 --> 00:48:40,842
You really are a virgin, right?

836
00:48:40,842 --> 00:48:42,139
Damn it, I said so, didn't I?

837
00:48:42,139 --> 00:48:43,681
Okay, okay. I got it.

838
00:48:43,681 --> 00:48:45,615
I'll pay, I will.

839
00:48:45,615 --> 00:48:46,662
How much?

840
00:48:46,662 --> 00:48:47,689
You...

841
00:48:47,689 --> 00:48:48,715
You're...

842
00:48:48,715 --> 00:48:50,706
You've done this before, haven't you?

843
00:48:50,706 --> 00:48:54,312
You seem alarmingly adept at this.
You've done this before, haven't you?

844
00:48:55,276 --> 00:48:57,518
Just give me a million won.

845
00:48:57,518 --> 00:49:00,559
I'm lowballing you here,
but only because I need the money.

846
00:49:00,559 --> 00:49:02,215
What the hell?

847
00:49:02,215 --> 00:49:03,421
A million?

848
00:49:03,421 --> 00:49:05,875
I can get a girl for
two or three hundred thousand around here!

849
00:49:05,875 --> 00:49:07,202
Mister.

850
00:49:07,202 --> 00:49:08,840
I'm pretty.

851
00:49:12,055 --> 00:49:13,559
Show me the money first.

852
00:49:13,559 --> 00:49:15,124
Only then will I start.

853
00:49:18,322 --> 00:49:19,427
Okay.

854
00:49:49,246 --> 00:49:53,022
Are you just that brave?

855
00:49:53,022 --> 00:49:55,355
Or are you just dumb?

856
00:49:55,355 --> 00:49:58,085
I don't have to do what you ask.

857
00:49:58,922 --> 00:50:01,803
These streets are literally right up my alley.

858
00:50:03,509 --> 00:50:05,009
So, what now?

859
00:50:05,009 --> 00:50:06,964
Take your clothes off.

860
00:50:08,955 --> 00:50:11,255
If you want this money, at least.

861
00:50:17,589 --> 00:50:20,455
Hey, and everything comes off, okay?

862
00:50:20,455 --> 00:50:21,695
Everything.

863
00:50:24,789 --> 00:50:26,502
You see, I'm...

864
00:50:26,502 --> 00:50:30,004
legally recognized as
having diminished capacity.

865
00:50:30,995 --> 00:50:33,013
So, if I just happened to get drunk
and did some stuff to you,

866
00:50:33,013 --> 00:50:36,439
I'll just go to jail for a few months
and that's the end of it.

867
00:50:37,602 --> 00:50:43,330
Which is why I've got balls of steel right now!

868
00:50:53,482 --> 00:50:55,249
You keep quiet, okay?

869
00:50:57,989 --> 00:50:59,318
Yeah, what's up?

870
00:51:03,735 --> 00:51:05,009
Hey.

871
00:51:05,009 --> 00:51:06,849
You better be naked and ready.

872
00:51:06,849 --> 00:51:08,487
Or I'll kill you.

873
00:51:12,042 --> 00:51:13,382
I'm listening.

874
00:51:15,002 --> 00:51:19,024
No, I dropped her off.
I'm back home and about to go to bed.

875
00:51:20,475 --> 00:51:21,659
I'm not lying.

876
00:51:21,659 --> 00:51:24,593
I was just about to go to sleep.

877
00:51:25,375 --> 00:51:27,013
I'm serious.

878
00:51:27,013 --> 00:51:28,997
Why are you calling me? I'm about to sleep.

879
00:51:28,997 --> 00:51:31,015
I'm tired.

880
00:51:31,015 --> 00:51:32,800
I said I'm not!

881
00:51:33,886 --> 00:51:36,308
Hey! Damn.

882
00:51:39,766 --> 00:51:41,536
Damn it!

883
00:51:42,715 --> 00:51:46,102
Tell them to go through Kim Nam Jun's room.

884
00:51:46,102 --> 00:51:47,462
Yeah.

885
00:51:47,462 --> 00:51:50,931
Um, and check Sung Sae Ryeong's room, too.

886
00:51:50,931 --> 00:51:53,290
Then search every inn
around here for all I care!

887
00:51:53,290 --> 00:51:55,751
They're both out of their minds.

888
00:51:55,751 --> 00:51:57,140
Damn.

889
00:51:57,851 --> 00:51:59,075
I'm hanging up.

890
00:51:59,764 --> 00:52:01,456
Dul Hee.

891
00:52:01,456 --> 00:52:04,140
It's been over an hour
since Sae Ryeong and Nam Jun left,

892
00:52:04,140 --> 00:52:06,123
but neither of them is anywhere to be seen.

893
00:52:06,822 --> 00:52:09,273
You don't think something happened, do you?

894
00:52:23,415 --> 00:52:24,430
What?

895
00:52:42,333 --> 00:52:43,749
Damn it!

896
00:52:46,885 --> 00:52:48,415
Where the hell is she?

897
00:53:13,113 --> 00:53:14,459
How'd it go?

898
00:53:14,459 --> 00:53:15,777
Have you found them?

899
00:53:15,777 --> 00:53:16,828
No, we haven't.

900
00:53:16,828 --> 00:53:20,792
But the girls said Nam Jun
took that Sae Ryeong girl to a motel,

901
00:53:20,792 --> 00:53:22,635
but she ran away.

902
00:53:27,009 --> 00:53:30,514
Hey, catch Kim Nam Jun and kill him!

903
00:53:31,693 --> 00:53:33,466
Which motel was it?

904
00:53:53,393 --> 00:53:56,102
I told you not to prey on minors!

905
00:53:57,366 --> 00:53:59,173
And even if she was an adult...

906
00:54:00,946 --> 00:54:03,760
you should just stay away from women!

907
00:54:03,760 --> 00:54:04,784
Stay back.

908
00:54:04,784 --> 00:54:06,121
- Put that down.
- Stay away!

909
00:54:06,121 --> 00:54:09,578
- I'll kill you if you come closer!
- Hey, put it down!

910
00:54:19,051 --> 00:54:20,906
Are you worried?

911
00:54:20,906 --> 00:54:21,956
No.

912
00:54:22,973 --> 00:54:24,493
Really?

913
00:54:24,493 --> 00:54:25,564
Yeah.

914
00:54:35,199 --> 00:54:37,990
How will we take Sae Ryeong with us?

915
00:55:12,673 --> 00:55:14,273
What's going on?

916
00:55:14,273 --> 00:55:15,753
Are you okay?

917
00:55:35,713 --> 00:55:37,203
- Hey.
- Let go.

918
00:55:37,203 --> 00:55:38,587
- Let go of me!
- Sung Sae Ryeong!

919
00:55:38,587 --> 00:55:39,719
Let me go!

920
00:55:39,719 --> 00:55:41,813
I said let go!

921
00:55:41,813 --> 00:55:43,636
Let go of me!

922
00:55:49,233 --> 00:55:50,763
Let go!

923
00:55:51,619 --> 00:55:52,792
Let me go!

924
00:55:52,792 --> 00:55:54,607
Please, stop this.

925
00:55:58,686 --> 00:55:59,710
Just stop.

926
00:55:59,710 --> 00:56:03,824
<i>Why did I think that
I could become a main character?</i>

927
00:56:06,906 --> 00:56:10,240
<i>Things like that never happen to me.</i>

928
00:56:11,256 --> 00:56:12,449
<i>Ha Yeon.</i>

929
00:56:16,726 --> 00:56:19,246
<i>On the train, Yu Gyeom asked me...</i>

930
00:56:21,359 --> 00:56:23,994
<i>if I'd go back home when summer break ended.</i>

931
00:56:28,126 --> 00:56:29,510
<i>And I...</i>

932
00:56:33,826 --> 00:56:36,095
<i>told him that I would.</i>

933
00:56:40,346 --> 00:56:42,126
<i>"Yes."</i>

934
00:56:42,126 --> 00:56:44,845
<i>"I'll go back to my normal life."</i>

935
00:56:46,826 --> 00:56:49,886
<i>"To my everyday life,
where the real me belongs."</i>

936
00:56:49,886 --> 00:56:55,490
<i>"To my life, where I'm more like a kettle
or a set of faded curtains."</i>

937
00:56:55,490 --> 00:56:57,805
<i>"So you should live yours, too."</i>

938
00:56:58,659 --> 00:57:02,473
<i>"That bright-red, vivid life of yours..."</i>

939
00:57:02,473 --> 00:57:06,989
<i>"where there isn't
even a place for me to invade."</i>

940
00:57:12,893 --> 00:57:15,076
<i>"I hope you're happy."</i>

941
00:57:16,436 --> 00:57:20,049
<i>But these words never left my lips,</i>

942
00:57:21,608 --> 00:57:26,274
<i>and all I could tell him was,
"Yes, I would go back."</i>
